{"id":"f9bce364-ed75-4aa8-94a5-4f1aedd66a36","object":"chat.completion","created":1785021449,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    round_scores = case['round_scores']\\n    round_targets = case['round_targets']\\n    forced = set(case['forced'])\\n    history = []\\n    for scores, target in zip(round_scores, round_targets):\\n        # Include forced indices\\n        selected = list(forced)\\n        # Build list of (score, index) for non-forced\\n        options = [(s, i) for i, s in enumerate(scores) if i not in forced]\\n        # Sort descending by score\\n        options.sort(reverse=True)\\n        # Take top (target - len(forced)) indices\\n        needed = target - len(forced)\\n        selected.extend([i for (_, i) in options[:needed]])\\n        # Sort for consistent output\\n        selected.sort()\\n        history.append(selected)\\n    # Retained indices: intersection of all rounds\\n    retained_set = set(history[0])\\n    for sel in history[1:]:\\n        retained_set &= set(sel)\\n    retained_indices = sorted(retained_set)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"history\\\": history,\\n        \\\"retained_indices\\\": retained_indices\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write Python code for solve(case) that returns a JSON object with \"history\" and \"retained_indices\". Based on task description: it's NLP-LLM-02. The payload has \"round_scores\", \"round_targets\", \"forced\". We need to interpret the problem. Likely it's about selecting indices from round_scores based on round_targets and forced. The \"history\" could be a list of tuples? Output schema: history is array of arrays of integers. retained_indices is array of integers. So we need to produce something.\n\nGiven the input: round_scores is list of lists (each inner list has 8 floats). round_targets is list of integers (length 2). forced is list of integers (length 1). Probably means: